Done. KLEE 3.1 is installed with STP as its solver, built against LLVM 16, with no uClibc.

**What was built (all under `/usr/local`, source in `/opt/src`)**

- **MiniSat** — STP needs its own fork; the distro's `minisat` 2.2.1 headers are incompatible. Built statically into `/usr/local/lib/libminisat.a`.
- **STP 2.3.4** — static `libstp.a`, `stp` binary, and a CMake package at `/usr/local/lib/cmake/STP`. CryptoMiniSat disabled: its Ubuntu headers clash with STP's `lbool` usage.
- **KLEE 3.1** — `ENABLE_SOLVER_STP=ON`, Z3/metaSMT off, `ENABLE_KLEE_UCLIBC` not used, POSIX runtime on.

**One thing I had to fix to make it work here:** this host is aarch64, and KLEE's POSIX runtime (`runtime/POSIX/fd.c`) hardcodes x86-only syscall names (`__NR_open`, `__NR_stat`, `__NR_lstat`, `__NR_access`, `__NR_select`, `__NR_chmod`, `__NR_chown`, `__NR_readlink`, `__NR_utimes`, `__NR_futimesat`), none of which exist in the asm-generic ABI. I added a `KLEE_ASM_GENERIC_SYSCALLS` guard that maps each to its `*at` equivalent (`openat`, `newfstatat` with `AT_SYMLINK_NOFOLLOW` for `lstat`, `faccessat`, `pselect6`, `fchmodat`, `fchownat`, `readlinkat`, `utimensat` with `timeval`→`timespec` conversion). The x86 paths are left untouched. Without this the runtime bitcode doesn't even compile.

**`~/.bashrc`** — a marked block *above* the `[ -z "$PS1" ] && return` early exit, so `source ~/.bashrc` works in the non-interactive shells the tests use. It exports `PATH`, `CPATH=/usr/local/include`, `LD_LIBRARY_PATH`, `STP_DIR`, each guarded with a `case` so repeated sourcing doesn't duplicate entries.

**Verification** (clean `env -i` shell sourcing `~/.bashrc`): `which klee` → `/usr/local/bin/klee`; `klee --version` → KLEE 3.1 / Ubuntu LLVM 16.0.6; `CPATH=/usr/local/include`; `stp --version` → 2.3.3. Compiled a program using `#include <klee/klee.h>` with only `CPATH` set (no `-I`), then ran it under `klee --posix-runtime` → "Using STP solver backend", test cases generated. `klee --help` lists `stp` as the default solver backend.

Two notes: I first tried a full-source `master` clone to see if the aarch64 fix already existed upstream — it doesn't, so I deleted that clone. Also, `klee` links STP statically, so it won't appear in `ldd`; the solver linkage is confirmed by the runtime output and the `--solver-backend` default.

